&lt;p&gt;The Field Marketing Manager owns the field-sourced and field-influenced pipeline contribution for a combination of products, turning webinars, third-party partnerships, conferences, and customer events into qualified meetings and pipeline for Workforce Compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an individual contributor role reporting to the Director of Demand Generation, Workforce Compliance Marketing. The Field Marketing Manager works hand in hand with SDRs and AEs so every program ends in sales follow-up, not just attendance. The role runs the planned calendar (webinars, events, newsletter placements) and the signal-triggered plays that sit on top of it (post-event retargeting, webinar re-engagement, account-based outreach).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role carries a named pipeline target for Workforce Compliance solutions, set with Sales and RevOps at the start of each quarter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline planning and reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a quarterly field plan for Workforce Compliance solutions that maps programs to the pipeline target, MQL quota, and Sales priorities, and review it with the Director and Sales leaders each quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report weekly on MQLs, hot leads, meetings, hot-meeting conversion, and pipeline created by program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend where to add, cut, or reshape programs based on pipeline per dollar and per program, and act on the decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Webinars and third-party partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and run Mitratech-hosted webinars and AMAs, partnering with Product Marketing on topics, content, and speakers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage third-party partners such as HR Morning, I Hate It Here, HR Brew, and HCI: placements, scheduling, co-hosted webinars, vendor budget, and a pipeline benchmark per partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Segment registrants into net-new and recycled, and tailor follow-up for each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Events and in-person programs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver conferences, regional events, executive roundtables, and prospect dinners, owning the pipeline plan from pre-event outreach through post-event follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get target lists to SDRs early to pre-book meetings, and run post-event retargeting from badge scans and registrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Customer Marketing to seat customer advocates at events and webinars, and with Partner Marketing on partner events and referrals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Events team on booth, logistics, and vendor execution so that this role stays focused on pipeline outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales and SDR follow-up&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own what happens to every lead after a program: routing, SDR and AE talk tracks, re-engagement sprints, and follow-up timing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track conversion from MQL to meeting to opportunity by program, and diagnose where it breaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet regularly with SDR leadership and AEs to learn what prospects are saying and adjust messaging and targeting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Route play-triggered leads directly to Sales with context, and measure each play against the pipeline it creates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Sell and Signal-triggered plays&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and run plays that fire on a signal rather than the calendar, such as multi-registrant accounts, webinar attendance, badge scans, and intent data from tools like 6sense, ZoomInfo, and Qualified.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build evergreen cross-sell programs between Workforce Compliance products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement, budget, and operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own campaign setup, naming, and source tagging in HubSpot and Salesforce, and reconcile attribution with RevOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable playbooks and templates, and use AI to speed up list building, personalization, follow-up, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements &amp;amp; Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in B2B field marketing, event marketing, or demand generation, with a record of contributing to a pipeline number.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience running in-person and virtual events and webinars as an individual contributor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with SDRs and AEs, and a clear understanding of how Sales motions turn leads into meetings and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to report pipeline sourced, pipeline influenced, and conversion rates, using Salesforce and HubSpot (campaigns, attribution, reports) and a webinar platform such as Goldcast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management and follow-through across multiple programs at once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working cross-functionally with Product Marketing, Content, Paid Media, Digital, ABM, Customer Marketing, and RevOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Day-to-day use of AI tools to speed up research, personalization, follow-up, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will disclose intended pay ranges in our job ads for US-based opportunities – This role can be performed 100% remote anywhere in the US. &lt;strong&gt;Anticipated Pay Range: $90,000 Annually USD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Total compensation includes US employee benefits and annual bonus eligibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits we offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health, Dental &amp;amp; Vision Insurance *&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401 (k) + Employer Match *&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open PTO + 11 Paid Holidays + 4 Annual Paid Global Wellness Days Off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;STD, LTD &amp;amp; Group Life Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pet Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FSA &amp;amp; HSA Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perks we offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote Work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career Advancement &amp;amp; Professional Development Opportunities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Recognition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LinkedIn Learning Platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mitratech is proud to be an EEOE, M/F/D/V, and we are committed to diversity both in practice and spirit at the corporate level.&amp;nbsp;Mitratech participates in the Electronic Employment Verification Program. E-Verify is an Internet-based system that compares information from an employee’s I-9 to data from the U.S. Department of Homeland Security and Social Security Administration Records. To learn more, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://everify.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;everify.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;strong style=&quot;padding: 0px; margin: 0px; font-family: Satoshi, &#39;Satoshi Fallback&#39;; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; vertical-align: baseline; overflow-wrap: break-word; color: var(--n800); font-style: normal; letter-spacing: normal; text-align: start; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;padding: 0px; margin: 0px; font-family: var(--font-family,&#39;sans-serif&#39;); border: 0px; font-size: 14px; vertical-align: baseline; overflow-wrap: break-word;&quot;&gt;We are an equal-opportunity employer that values diversity at all levels. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, national origin, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, or veteran status.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MyFitnessPal is investing in creators as a scalable growth channel. As Influencer Marketing Manager, you will lead the day-to-day execution of our influencer program while owning how we measure its success and demonstrate its return on investment. You will manage a team of influencer specialists and work directly with talent, agents, and internal partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Day-to-day execution&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee creator communications and provide hands-on support throughout the partnership lifecycle, from outreach and onboarding to briefing, content delivery, payment and performance analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain long-term relationships with creators, talent managers, and agencies to drive loyalty, preferred rates, and repeat partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate incoming and proposed influencer deals, determining which are worth pursuing based on audience fit, performance potential, and cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage relationships with celebrity and macro influencers, including negotiation oversight and content planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review creator content to ensure it meets brand standards, messaging requirements, and campaign objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track influencer performance against established KPIs and report results to stakeholders on a regular cadence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Program management&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage influencer budgets and allocate spend across creators, tiers, and platforms to maximize return&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams (e.g., Brand, Product Marketing, Growth Marketing, Legal, Finance) to support ongoing marketing campaigns and integrate creator activity into broader plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop influencer specialists who negotiate creator contracts, setting priorities, deal guidelines, and quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve existing automations and build new automated processes (e.g., outreach, tracking, reporting, payments) to increase team efficiency and scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strategy and measurement&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop influencer strategies and programs aligned with overall brand and business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research industry trends, emerging platforms, and competitor activity, and translate findings into actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine how we define and measure program success, including the KPIs, benchmarks, and reporting framework used across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own our approach to conversion measurement, including attribution methodology and tracking tools, so creator activity can be credibly tied to downstream results such as installs, trials, and paid subscriptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7 years of experience in influencer, creator, or social media marketing, including experience managing celebrity or macro talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing budgets and negotiating or overseeing creator contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or mentoring team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, with experience in attribution, performance reporting, and ROI analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, relationship-building, and negotiation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of TikTok, Instagram, and YouTube creator ecosystems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in health, fitness, nutrition, or consumer subscription apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with mobile measurement partners, affiliate platforms, and creator management tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI tools and automations a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Exciting Full-Time Employee Benefits, Perks and Culture&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Face-to-Face Connections&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; We value personal connections. Enjoy opportunities to meet and connect with your team members in person to help forge meaningful relationships that extend beyond the virtual realm. Teams meet as often as needed and all of MyFitnessPal gathers annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibility At Its Best:&lt;/strong&gt; Achieve the work-life balance you deserve. Enjoy a flexible time-off policy with our &lt;em&gt;Responsible Time Off &lt;/em&gt;benefit.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Give Back:&lt;/strong&gt; Use&amp;nbsp; your volunteer days off to support what matters most to you. Each full time teammate receives 2 days per calendar year to give back to their community through service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentorship Program:&lt;/strong&gt; Take control of your career through our mentorship program where, if you’d like, you will be matched with a teammate who can help you scale your skills and propel your growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Family-Friendly Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; Embrace the journey with confidence and care. Enjoy our paid maternity and paternity leave, to provide time to balance family responsibilities with your career and take the time needed to strengthen family relationships.&amp;nbsp; We understand the complexities of starting or expanding a family, which is why we provide best-in-class comprehensive assistance for fertility-related matters.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellness Comes First&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; Live Good Health is one of our core values. Receive a monthly Wellness Allowance, empowering you to focus on your physical and mental well-being by choosing from a range of wellness initiatives, including dedicated mental health days.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Celebrate Greatness:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Your hard work deserves recognition! Our reward and recognition platform empowers peers to acknowledge and reward each other for the exceptional contributions they make.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elevate Your Health &amp;amp; Fitness:&lt;/strong&gt; Get access to MyFitnessPal Premium, allowing you to take your fitness, health and wellness journey to new heights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unlock Your Potential:&lt;/strong&gt; Access our virtual learning and development library, and participate in training opportunities&amp;nbsp; to continuously grow and enhance your skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Championing Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;: Our dedicated DEI Committee actively fosters a diverse and inclusive workplace by setting actionable goals and evaluating progress across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Healthcare Matters:&lt;/strong&gt; Your well-being is our priority. Take advantage of our competitive medical, dental, and vision benefits that cater to your holistic healthcare needs. Feel secure and supported on your wellness journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Your Future:&lt;/strong&gt; Benefit from our retirement savings program, giving you peace of mind for your financial goals. Reach them sooner with MyFitnessPal’s competitive employer match.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At MyFitnessPal, our mission is to enable people to make healthy choices. And it wouldn&#39;t be possible without our team. We celebrate the unique POV that each person brings to the table and believe in a collaborative and inclusive environment. As an equal opportunity employer, we prohibit any unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, religion, military or veteran status, sex, gender, marital status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, age, or disability. These are our guiding ideologies and apply across all aspects of employment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MyFitnessPal participates in E-Verify.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Keep Growing with Nutrafol&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;description__text&quot; data-test-description-text=&quot;&quot;&gt;We’re a growing company. Everything we do, we do to help people grow into the best version of themselves. As the pioneers of hair wellness, we create clinically tested products for hair growth and provide support for people at every step of their hair journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;description__text&quot; data-test-description-text=&quot;&quot;&gt;Our multi-factorial approach targets key root causes of hair thinning using a patented blend of standardized vitamins, minerals and natural ingredients -- and is recommended by over 7,500 physicians and hair professionals for trusted, reliable results. We never settle, and are continuously challenging existing treatments and methodologies to advance the frontier of hair science. As we help our customers grow, we grow too -- by embracing individuality and differences, leading by example, and empowering ourselves and others with our passion for wellness and innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;description__text&quot; data-test-description-text=&quot;&quot;&gt;Keep growing. It’s our mantra. Our commitment to helping anybody and everybody committed to realizing their own potential to grow.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Development &amp;amp; Marketing Manager is a hands-on product innovation marketer who will help shape what we launch next. Sitting within the Product Development &amp;amp; Marketing team, this role turns consumer insights, clinical science and market trends into new products and line extensions across our dietary supplement and topical hair care portfolios, and guides them from early concept through stage-gate development to launch and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting into the Sr. Manager of Product Development &amp;amp; Marketing, this role works across a dynamic portfolio of projects rather than a single fixed category, moving between dietary supplements and topical cosmetic innovation as business priorities evolve. You will partner closely with Brand Marketing, Consumer Insights, Education, Growth, Retention, Retail, Professional, Creative, Copy, Formulation, Packaging, Operations, Supply Chain, Regulatory, Legal, Quality and Clinical &amp;amp; Medical Affairs, serving as the day-to-day contact who keeps each project on strategy, on time and on budget across our multi-channel business, including direct to consumer, Amazon, healthcare professionals, salons and prestige retail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive Landscape &amp;amp; Innovation Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the competitive landscape from the product perspective, tracking competitor launches, formulations, ingredients, claims, clinical results, pricing and packaging across supplement and topical hair care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a centralized competitive intelligence hub, including product benchmarks, claims and ingredient matrices and pricing architecture, that serves as the single source of truth for the team and cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Sr. Manager and Consumer Insights team to bring consumer research together with competitive and product intelligence, organizing the combined view into clear opportunity assessments and product recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver regular competitive readouts that flag threats and whitespace, and use them to inform the innovation pipeline and roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build compelling business cases for new concepts, including market sizing, consumer rationale, pricing, volume forecasts and margin targets, to secure stage-gate approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Development &amp;amp; Stage-Gate:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute the stage-gate process and all deliverables for assigned projects across supplements and topicals, from ideation and concept through development, commercialization and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write product, creative and copy briefs, defining the target consumer, benefits, claims ambition, format and cost targets, grounded in competitive benchmarks and product differentiation as approved by leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop product claims in partnership with Formulation and Clinical &amp;amp; Medical Affairs, grounded in how ingredients and studies support efficacy. Own them through Regulatory and Legal review to final approval for packaging, marketing and launch materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive feasibility reviews with Packaging, Operations and Supply Chain for each concept. Confirm it can be manufactured, scaled and hit target cost of goods (COGS) and margin before each stage gate, and resolve any issues that would affect launch timing, raising risks to leadership as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Positioning, Claims &amp;amp; Go-to-Market:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop product positioning, value propositions, naming direction and core messaging that set new launches apart from the competition, aligning with senior Product and Brand leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape claims strategy in partnership with Clinical &amp;amp; Medical Affairs and Regulatory, ensuring structure/function and cosmetic claims are compelling, substantiated and compliant with FDA, FTC and NAD guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development of new product assets that communicate efficacy and results (clinical before/afters, certification content, testing content, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build integrated go-to-market plans with Brand Marketing, Growth, Retention, Retail and Professional teams, tailoring launch strategies by channel and audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brief Creative, Copy and Packaging teams on launch assets that communicate efficacy, including clinical before-and-afters and testing content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Education to create sell-in materials, product training and FAQs for retail partners, healthcare professionals, stylists and Customer Experience teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Medical Affairs to ensure clinical and scientific validation is reflected accurately in marketing communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Launch Performance &amp;amp; Lifecycle Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track post-launch performance against defined KPIs and competitive response, sharing learnings and recommending adjustments to positioning, claims or assortment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In partnership with the Sr. Manager, identify opportunities to strengthen the existing portfolio through reformulations, line extensions, new formats and updated claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory &amp;amp; Quality Partnership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Regulatory Affairs and Quality Assurance on compliance and product certifications for both dietary supplements and topical/cosmetic products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proof packaging artwork and copy for accuracy, regulatory compliance and brand alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in product development, innovation and/or product marketing within supplements, OTC, beauty or personal care; hair care or skincare preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of taking products from concept to launch through a cross-functional stage-gate process, ideally across omnichannel businesses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience conducting competitive analysis and product benchmarking, with the ability to organize complex market and consumer information into clear, actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen, including building business cases, forecasts and pricing recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of claims substantiation and regulatory considerations for structure/function and/or cosmetic claims (FDA, FTC &amp;amp; NAD), including taking claims through Regulatory and Legal review&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing product, creative and copy briefs that drive clear, on-strategy work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex scientific and technical information into clear, compelling, consumer-friendly language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized and detail-oriented; thrives managing multiple projects and shifting priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel and PowerPoint skills; SPINS, Circana or Amazon data experience a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication and cross-functional collaboration skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;Nutrafol takes into consideration a wide range of factors in final compensation decisions, including but not limited to: skill sets, experience and training, licensure and certifications, qualifications and education, and other business and organizational needs. The listed range is applicable only to the annual base salary and does not include additional perks, benefits, or applicable bonus eligibility comprising the total compensation package.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$120,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$130,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nutrafol is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants without regard to race, religion, color, sex, pregnancy (including breast feeding and related medical conditions), national origin, citizenship status, uniform service member status, age, genetic information, disability, and for employees working in California, ancestry, ethnicity, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, marital status, protected medical condition, or any other protected status in accordance with all applicable federal, state and local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perks &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully remote work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision package, including FSA/HSA program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quarterly Bonus Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Two company-wide wellness breaks every day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free lunch on us every Tuesday and Thursday via Seamless/Grubhub&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly wellness stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly internet stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly cell phone stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual learning &amp;amp; development stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free meditation app membership (Headspace)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free monthly Nutrafol subscription&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pet insurance discounts and benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;California residents may review our CCPA notice &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/e/2PACX-1vQZ6uqrFPkPGgoxOBZ_yGalkC5BeQQCNfm5y-7lgIHXP-bX6c7sh5PnuXJy09uSLQ/pub&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Omada Health is on a mission to bend the curve of chronic disease.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Omada Health is looking for an experienced product marketing leader to help us win in GLP-1 and cardiometabolic health. This role supports our new program development marketing, including GLP-1 solutions, with an emphasis on differentiated positioning, commercial execution, and bringing new offerings to market. This is a hands-on player-coach role with one direct report. Your primary focus will be leading strategy and personally delivering high-impact work, complemented by focused coaching and development of a product marketer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;You will be a strategic partner to commercial, product, and clinical leadership, translating buyer needs, competitive dynamics, and field insights into a clear, compelling reason to choose Omada. You will own product messaging, go-to-market strategy, and support sales enablement, helping our teams connect the right offering and value story to each buyer’s priorities. Your highest priorities will be buyer and offer clarity through developing positioning and value stories by segment and asset development with a fast market-to-field feedback loop that increases selling effectiveness.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;At the center of this role is a continuous feedback loop between the field and our value story. You will work closely with sales, consultant relations, and other channel and customer-facing teams to understand what resonates and why we win or lose. You will turn those insights into stronger messaging, more effective sales tools, and recommendations that inform product and commercial strategy, then bring those improvements back to the field and assess what works.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relevant experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 10+ years of experience in B2B marketing, including 5+ years in healthcare and life sciences. Experience in virtual care, digital health, health plans, PBMs, or pharma is preferred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial judgment:&lt;/strong&gt; A track record of shaping product marketing strategies that help sales teams compete and win in complex, multi-stakeholder buying processes. You understand how employers, health plans, PBMs, and benefits consultants evaluate clinical and economic value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product marketing craft:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated strength in buyer research, competitive intelligence, positioning, messaging, go-to-market planning, product launches, and sales enablement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic and hands-on execution:&lt;/strong&gt; You can set a clear direction and personally build the presentation, business case narrative, competitive response, or launch messaging needed to move the work forward. You&#39;ve done this on a lean team, delivering field-ready work in weeks, not quarters.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience working directly with sales and customer-facing teams to turn deal-level feedback into actionable insights, stronger value stories, and repeatable approaches to selling.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compelling storytelling:&lt;/strong&gt; The ability to translate complex clinical, product, and economic information into clear, credible content tailored to different buyers and stakeholders.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; The ability to influence decisions, facilitate productive feedback, and align teams across commercial, product, clinical, and marketing without relying on formal authority.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People development:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience directly managing and developing marketing talent, with a willingness to balance coaching one direct report with substantial individual contribution.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience defining KPIs and using qualitative and quantitative feedback to assess buyer understanding, field readiness, competitive conversion, and adoption, rather than simply counting materials produced.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree in a related field.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;You will help turn Omada’s GLP-1 and cardiometabolic strategy into a differentiated commercial story that drives selling effectiveness. Success means buyers understand our value, the field is equipped to win the right opportunities, and eligible members receive a clear, consistent explanation of the care available to them.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market sensing that drives action:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Run a regular win/loss forum that incorporates competitive feedback.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Facilitate a fast feedback loop across Sales, Consultant Relations, channel teams, Product Marketing, and Strategy. Translate signals into clear recommendations about what has changed and what we should do differently, not simply market updates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with Product and Clinical to translate programs and analysis into messaging implications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Close the loop by bringing updated messaging and tools back to the field, pilot in select deals, and using the results to guide further improvements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Buyer segmentation and differentiated positioning:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Set annual product marketing priorities for how Omada wins in GLP-1 and cardiometabolic health: who we target, which problems we solve, and why buyers should choose us over alternatives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Work through a broader B2B and Brand Marketing organization to drive awareness of your program segments and strategy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Develop distinct value stories for employers covering GLP-1s and those not covering them, and for buyers prioritizing cost management versus population health. Support segment adaptation for consultant and payers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Maintain one coherent Omada portfolio narrative, with differentiated reasons to buy across audiences, offerings, and channels.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with Clinical and Thought Leadership to translate evidence into relevant proof points and identify evidence gaps that matter to purchasing decisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offer clarity and the buyer business case:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Turn capabilities into understandable, purchasable offers that clearly explain what is included, who qualifies, how access works, who pays, and what value is supported by evidence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Co-develop packaging and pricing recommendations, comparison and business-case tools, and guarantee messaging with Product, Finance, Strategy, and commercial partners.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Ensure clinical and economic claims are clear and credible, explicitly distinguishing observed results from modeled savings and explaining relevant assumptions and limitations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales and channel effectiveness:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Personally build and refine the narrative, pitch decks, discovery guides, competitive responses, proof points, and support business-case tools that help the field sell effectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with sales leaders on priority opportunities, tailoring the value story and addressing clinical, operational, and economic objections. Turn successful approaches into repeatable tools and practices.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Equip consultants, PBMs, and other channel partners with a compelling reason and a practical way to sell Omada, including channel-specific messaging, use cases, and materials that fit their selling process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with Customer Effectiveness on practical training, and test messaging and tools in real buyer conversations rather than treating delivery of an asset as the finish line.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Launch readiness and continuous adaptation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Support commercial readiness for new GLP-1 and cardiometabolic offerings, not just announcement day, aligning the offer, messaging, evidence, training, channel materials, and member communications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Lead product marketing’s launch planning and post-launch optimization, with clear cross-functional responsibilities and feedback from early selling and member experiences.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Keep messaging and tools current as capabilities, evidence, and market conditions change.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead as a player-coach:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Manage and develop one product marketer, setting clear priorities, providing regular feedback, and supporting growth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Maintain direct ownership of strategic initiatives and core deliverables, modeling strong product marketing craft and close partnership with the field.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Competitive salary with generous annual cash bonus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Equity grants&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Employee stock purchasing plan (ESPP)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Remote first work from home culture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Flexible Time Off to help you rest, recharge, and connect with loved ones&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Generous parental leave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Health, dental, and vision insurance (and above market employer contributions)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;401k retirement savings plan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Lifestyle Spending Account (LSA)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Mental Health Support Solutions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;...and more!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;It takes a village to change health care. As we build together toward our mission, we strive to embody the following values in our day-to-day work. We hope these hold meaning for you as well as you consider Omada!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cultivate Trust.&lt;/strong&gt; We listen closely and we operate with kindness. We provide respectful and candid feedback to each other.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seek Context. &lt;/strong&gt;We ask to understand and we build connections. We do our research up front to move faster down the road.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act Boldly.&lt;/strong&gt; We innovate daily to solve problems, improve processes, and find new opportunities for our members and customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver Results. &lt;/strong&gt;We reward impact above output. We set a high bar, we’re not afraid to fail, and we take pride in our work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Succeed Together. &lt;/strong&gt;We prioritize Omada’s progress above team or individual. We have fun as we get stuff done, and we celebrate together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remember Why We’re Here.&lt;/strong&gt; We push through the challenges of changing health care because we know the destination is worth it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Omada Health:&lt;/strong&gt; Omada Health (Nasdaq: OMDA) is reverse engineering the way healthcare is delivered in America, putting the space between doctor visits–where health is won or lost–at the center of care. Today&#39;s healthcare system poorly serves chronic conditions that require ongoing support outside of the exam room, like obesity, diabetes, hypertension, cholesterol, and musculoskeletal conditions. Omada’s virtual-first model combines human-led care teams, connected devices, and AI-enabled technology to deliver personalized care at scale, including support for GLP-1 therapy. Omada has served more than two million members since launch across 2,000+ employers, health plans, pharmacy benefit managers, and health systems. Learn more at omadahealth.com.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Omada is thrilled to share that we’ve been certified as a Great Place to Work! Please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.greatplacetowork.com/certified-company/7022924&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;We carefully hire the best talent we can find, which means actively seeking diversity of beliefs, backgrounds, education, and ways of thinking. We strive to build an inclusive culture where differences are celebrated and leveraged to inform better design and business decisions. Omada is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal opportunity regardless of race, color, religion, sex, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, physical or mental disability, legally protected medical condition, family care status, military or veteran status, marital status, domestic partner status, sexual orientation, or any other basis protected by local, state, or federal laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Below is a summary of salary ranges, by geographic zone, for this role*. These ranges represent a good faith estimate of the minimum and maximum base salary for the position in that zone at the time of posting. Please refer to this&lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/file/d/14E-cuIgPhwmVeVg3UdhzqhOYqeu-pTEU/view?usp=sharing&quot;&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.omadahealth.com/hubfs/Hiring%20Documents/Omada_Salary_Zones.pdf&quot;&gt;resource&lt;/a&gt; for detail on zone designations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zone 1: $194,120 - $242,650&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zone 2: $185,680 - $232,100&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zone 3: $168,800 - $211,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that zones may be updated as market data changes but we will honor the range applicable to your zone (which is determined by your location) as of your application date.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*The actual offer, including the compensation package, will be within the posted range for the relevant zone and will be determined based on multiple factors, such as the candidate&#39;s skills and experience, and other business considerations such as internal equity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.omadahealth.com/applicant-specific-notice&quot;&gt;click here &lt;/a&gt;for more information on our Candidate Privacy Notice.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Pinterest:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Millions of people around the world come to our platform to find creative ideas, dream about new possibilities and plan for memories that will last a lifetime. At Pinterest, we’re on a mission to bring everyone the inspiration to create a life they love, and that starts with the people behind the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Discover a career where you ignite innovation for millions, transform passion into growth opportunities, celebrate each other’s unique experiences and embrace the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/our-life/pinflex/&quot;&gt;flexibility&lt;/a&gt; to do your best work. Creating a career you love? It’s Possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Pinterest, AI isn&#39;t just a feature, it&#39;s a powerful partner that augments our creativity and amplifies our impact, and we’re looking for candidates who are excited to be a part of that. To get a complete picture of your experience and abilities, we’ll explore your foundational skills and how you collaborate with AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through our interview process, what matters most is that you can always explain your approach, showing us not just what you know, but how you think. You can read more about our AI interview philosophy and how we use AI in our recruiting process &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/our-philosophy-on-ai-in-hiring/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This role owns how Pinterest shows up with key industry associations and on the industry&#39;s biggest stages, like Cannes Lions and Pinterest Presents. You&#39;ll be the connective tissue between Pinterest&#39;s leaders and the external industry across global tentpoles, shaping visibility, influence and reputation across the advertising and marketing landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate brings strong integrated marketing expertise, excellent judgment, and the ability to lead through influence across a wide range of cross-functional partners. You are equally comfortable setting direction, shaping narratives, and driving excellent execution against high-priority business objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Pinterest’s industry presence, including executive speaking opportunities, external storytelling, and thought leadership at priority global tentpoles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop programming for Pinterest-owned events and global industry tentpoles, including talking points, fireside chats, client panels, testimonial videos, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inform Pinterest&#39;s speakership strategy and lead execution across key global tentpoles— including Cannes Lions and Pinterest Presents — sourcing, pitching and securing speaking opportunities that match the right Pinterest voices to the right stages and ladder up to business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional collaboration across regional and global stakeholders to align on priority opportunities, streamline execution, and deliver high-impact industry programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and support internal spokespeople and executives for speaking engagements, developing briefs, talking points and narratives in partnership with Comms to establish a consistent, compelling Pinterest story across every stage moment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and activate integrated partnership opportunities with clients and third-party partners that strengthen Pinterest’s industry relevance and contribute to business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end planning across briefs, workbacks, budgets, approvals, dependencies, logistics, and launch readiness to ensure programs are delivered with excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support measurement and optimization by defining success metrics, tracking program impact, and translating results into actionable recaps and recommendations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of industry and competitive trends to identify opportunities for Pinterest to lead timely, relevant conversations with senior brand and agency decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI to accelerate research, speaker briefing prep, event planning and reporting, while applying judgment and verification to establish correctness and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 8 years of experience in integrated marketing, B2B marketing, product marketing, brand marketing, and/or digital marketing, ideally within technology, media, advertising, agency, or platform environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and leading multi-channel marketing programs from strategy through execution, measurement, and optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the needs of advertisers, agencies, and sales organizations, with experience partnering closely with client-facing and revenue-driving teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or supporting high-profile industry moments such as tentpole events, executive speaking engagements, hosted events, thought leadership programs, and strategic partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex, cross-functional initiatives and influence outcomes across diverse stakeholders and functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic thinking paired with excellent operational rigor and project management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to shape narratives, build alignment, and communicate effectively with senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership, initiative, and sound judgment, with the ability to move work forward independently while navigating ambiguity and change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and a high bar for quality, with the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI tools to accelerate workflows across research, drafting, synthesis, analysis, planning, and reporting, paired with strong judgment to validate accuracy, mitigate bias, and maintain ownership of final outputs in line with Pinterest’s AI expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in marketing, communications, business or a related field or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relocation Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is not eligible for relocation assistance. Visit our PinFlex page to learn more about our working model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Office Requirement Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
